Licence of the files in this pack (qwen3-4b-q8)
================================================

pack.json, template.tpl
    Part of judgly, Apache License 2.0 (see LICENSE at the top of the judgly
    source tree or in the wheel's .dist-info/licenses/).

heads/h2.bin and heads/temperature.bin (the general calibration options, "*"),
when present
    Apache License 2.0. h2.bin is a small calibration head (a few hundred
    thousand numbers) and temperature.bin holds three numbers (one temperature
    per question type), both fitted on the model's answer-letter logits for
    items from the datasets below, all under permissive licences. The head contains no dataset text.
    Where a fitted head counts as an adaptation of the data, these works are
    used under their licences and are credited here:

      MMLU (Hendrycks et al. 2021)                  MIT
      CommonsenseQA (Talmor et al. 2019)            MIT
      StrategyQA (Geva et al. 2021)                 MIT
      HH-RLHF (Bai et al. 2022, Anthropic)          MIT
      QASC (Khot et al. 2020, AI2)                  CC BY 4.0
      Cosmos QA (Huang et al. 2019)                 CC BY 4.0
      BANKING77 (Casanueva et al. 2020, PolyAI)     CC BY 4.0
      Civil Comments (Borkan et al. 2019, Jigsaw)   CC0 1.0
      GoEmotions (Demszky et al. 2020, Google)      Apache 2.0
      HelpSteer2 (Wang et al. 2024, NVIDIA)         CC BY 4.0
      LEDGAR (Tuggener et al. 2020), as released    CC BY 4.0
        in LexGLUE (Chalkidis et al. 2022)
      judgly's own generated tasks                  Apache 2.0

    Changes: items were reformatted into multiple-choice, yes/no or score
    questions and only the model's logits on them were used; no text is
    redistributed. CC BY 4.0: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
    Evidence for each licence: docs/licences.md in the judgly repository.

heads/h2-stance.bin and heads/temperature-stance.bin (the stance calibration
options, "stance"), when present
    Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0),
    NOT Apache 2.0. Full text: LICENSES/CC-BY-SA-4.0.txt, and
    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/legalcode
    Both are fitted on items from share-alike data, so they are released under
    a share-alike licence as the conservative reading of those licences:

      MultiNLI (Williams, Nangia and Bowman 2018)   OANC licence, with parts
                                                    under CC BY-SA 3.0 and
                                                    CC BY 3.0 (see the card)
      VitaminC (Schuster, Fisch and Barzilay 2021)  CC BY-SA 3.0; contains
                                                    material derived from
                                                    Wikipedia (Wikipedia
                                                    contributors, CC BY-SA
                                                    3.0 / 4.0)
      FEVER (Thorne et al. 2018), gold evidence     CC BY-SA 3.0; evidence
        as released by Atanasova, Wright and        sentences from Wikipedia
        Augenstein (2020)                           (Wikipedia contributors)
      SNLI (Bowman et al. 2015, Stanford NLP)       CC BY-SA 4.0; includes
                                                    Flickr30k captions (Young
                                                    et al. 2014, CC BY-SA)
      WANLI (Liu et al. 2022)                       CC BY 4.0
      SciNLI (Sadat and Caragea 2022)               CC BY-SA 4.0

    CC BY-SA 3.0 section 4(b) allows adaptations to be licensed under a later
    version with the same licence elements, which is why 4.0 is used.
    Changes: items were reformatted into supports / refutes / not enough
    information questions and only the model's logits on them were used; no
    text is redistributed. Copyright of the heads: Timo Lassmann, 2026.

The model weights are NOT part of this pack. They are downloaded from
https://huggingface.co/unsloth/Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507-GGUF (GGUF conversion
by Unsloth of Qwen/Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507 by the Qwen team, Alibaba Cloud),
under the Apache License 2.0. "Qwen" names the model only; no endorsement by
Alibaba Cloud or the Qwen team is implied.
